        {
            "number": 3,
            "revision": "11988f7cb3367e3e1c01e58df197511cf45fdc6a",
            "parents": [
                "849eddc89ef8c0e2a82f9a18c4b08df5ac9b0179"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/23/89223/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "mikehqt",
                "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                "username": "mikehqt"
            },
            "createdOn": 1776995601,
            "author": {
                "name": "mikehqt",
                "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                "username": "mikehqt"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE_WITH_MESSAGE_UPDATE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "So, this is specifically to fix a case where the BMC enters \"NotReady\" after it was previously \"Ready\"?  As part of a BMC reboot?\n\nThat to me _is_ unexpected.  The BMC was ready and it is only \"not ready\" because it is shutting down, but I would not expect it to go to \"NotReady\" state for that.  Maybe \"Quiesed\" or \"Quiesing\".\n\nMaybe @geissonator@yahoo.com can give some clarity."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 13,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, exactly. The BMC is initially in the Ready state, and then transitions to NotReady after a reboot is triggered via D-Bus/Redfish."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "But the BMC is NotReady at that point of time.  Why is it \"undesirable\" or \"inconsistent\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "#21"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It is, isn't it?  That's the current behavior."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I agree that it works as expected."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why would the type of reboot affect this?  Isn't it entirely a race condition between the service starting up and the rest of the services starting?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 21,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "You are correct; the startup process is working exactly as expected during boot. Regarding the CLI behavior, the reason it doesn't generate the log is likely because the standard reboot command bypasses the D-Bus/Redfish graceful shutdown flow, thereby avoiding the state manager's transition logic entirely."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Isn't this a very heavy hammer though?  It means we _never_ get a NotReady even if it might be a true condition ...\n\nTo recap/clarify:\n- If bmc-state-manager starts before multi-user.target completes, we emit NotReady and then Ready.  This seems ok.\n- If bmc-state-manager starts as multi-user.target complets, we emit only Ready.  This is also ok even though \"inconsistent\".\n- If the BMC is in the process of rebooting, due to a user requires, I would not expect any new event to happen as part of that reboot except maybe an [new?] explicit \"Rebooting\" state."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 25,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the detailed review and clarification. Your recap makes perfect sense, and I agree with your assessment.\nYou are right. The root cause isn't that the event is being logged, but rather that the BMC is transitioning to NotReady during a shutdown/reboot sequence at all. My current patch only hides the symptom (the log) instead of fixing the inappropriate state transition.\nBased on your feedback, it seems the correct approach is to prevent currentBMCState from transitioning to NotReady if the system is already processing a shutdown or reboot request. As you mentioned, introducing a new state like Rebooting.\nSince Andrew is tagged, I'd appreciate his or your thoughts on whether we should \nintroduce a Rebooting state for this specific phase?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm still not a huge fan of this, it feels like we're working around something I wasn't super happy to begin with (the log on every state change). Going to NotReady on a reboot was added because at least at IBM, our external Redfish clients kept hitting a window during the BMC reboot where they thought the BMC was still \"Ready\" and was expecting normal Redfish API's to keep working. BMC reboots take 10-15s and bmcweb is the last to get shut down so it was a mess. Going to NotReady is an indicator to external clients to stop talking to the BMC in these reboot paths. \n\nBut with all that said, add a comment to the code and I'm fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 151,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Geissler",
                        "email": "geissonator@yahoo.com",
                        "username": "geissonator"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd like a comment addressing why we're directly calling the sdbusplus class here so we don't forget in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "bmc_state_manager.cpp",
                    "line": 151,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "mikehqt",
                        "email": "mike_hsieh@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "mikehqt"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the background. That context about the Redfish client and bmcweb hutdown timing is really helpful. I've updated the code with a comment explaining why we are transitioning to NotReady and why we're calling sdbusplus directly to bypass the startup-focused logging. This should ensure the 'why' isn't lost in the future."
                }
            ],
